{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/566238-loyalist-seeming-courts","id":566238,"title":"Loyalist Seeming/Courts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-24T04:47:04-07:00","id":566238,"title":"Loyalist Seeming/Courts","content":"Someone suggested this deserved its own topic so as it is written, so shall it be done!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T05:00:50-07:00","id":566263,"title":"","content":"I can see Loyalist Freehold with Courts being based on a Motley of True Fae, with each True Fae in the Motley getting a Court dedicated to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T05:13:42-07:00","id":566270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/566238-loyalist-seeming-courts?p=566263#post566263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see Loyalist Freehold with Courts being based on a Motley of True Fae, with each True Fae in the Motley getting a Court dedicated to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be particularily awesome if only the monarchs knew about this deal, and the rest of the members of the court as just random freeholders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T05:28:44-07:00","id":566274,"title":"","content":"If there was a Loyalist court, they would probably be the equivalent to the crime syndicate, as opposed to true members of the Free Holds. They lurk on the pathways of the Hedge, raiding travelers and hollows to appease their Keepers, and running various operations that oppose the prosperity and good nature of the Free Hold itself. They'd be recognized a Court in so far that they're an organized group, but it's not a Court any member of the Free Hold would actually want to interact with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Court of Supplicants</b>:<br /> <br /> <b>Emotion:</b> Submission<br /> <br /> <b>Info: </b>Whether forced into service or doing it of their own free will, the Court of Supplicants are Changelings who remain in the service of their Keepers and strive to appease them with their actions. If the rest of the Free Hold is comprised of kings, knights, and upstanding members of society, the Court of Supplicants are the bandits, thieves, murderers and other cast offs who failed to live up to society's expectations. The only rules they play by now are the ancient and unfathomable whims of the True Fae. The Court of Supplicants are not openly welcomed in Free Hold society, and so they choose to live on the outskirts. They lay traps along the paths of the Hedge, ambushing travelers and raiding the surrounding Hollows. If they're lucky, their victims are killed in the initial attack. If they're less fortunate, they could find themselves chained and dragged off to the slave market.<br /> <br /> Although they are outcasts, the Supplicants have one significant advantage over the rest of the Free Holds; they can recruit new members at will! The other Courts must wait for a Changeling to escape the Hedge and then vie against each other for their membership. The Supplicants, on the other hand, simply need to grab a human and drag them back to their Keeper for a bit of brainwashing.<br /> <br /> This ability to recruit members in such a way ensures the Supplicants can easily replenish their fallen numbers, and remain a constant threat, despite the efforts of the Free Holds to clear them out.<br /> <br /> If the Supplicants do have anything that resembles a hierarchy structure, it is not publicly known to the rest of the Free Holds. Like a crime syndicate, they put on a front of being proud and upstanding members of society. Donating to charity and all that crap, but when they are away from prying eyes, they conduct their true business of illegal activities. Silencing witnesses, extorting the vulnerable for protection money, selling cursed foods and equipment. All dedicated to the purpose of breaking your will to fight back. They feed on submission, and they will do whatever they can get away with to get the point across that you can't beat them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-24-2015, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T06:06:24-07:00","id":566287,"title":"","content":"I don't know about Loyalist Courts... I mean, they have their allegiance to their specific Keeper. That's their story. Their story isn't one of keeping the Gentry and Huntsmen at bay; in a real way, they're extensions of the Gentry and Huntsmen. How would rituals help them here? They don't develop approaches, they use approaches the freehold make. <br /> <br /> I guess what I'm asking is, what's the point of a Loyalist Court? Just the mantle and affinity Contracts? <br /> <br /> <br /> As for seeming... <br /> I think we've all got a fair grasp on what the flavor of a loyalist would be. We just need the crunch - clarity points and contracts. And without those two, I don't know if there's much that can be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T06:26:15-07:00","id":566293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/566238-loyalist-seeming-courts?p=566287#post566287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about Loyalist Courts... I mean, they have their allegiance to their specific Keeper. That's their story. Their story isn't one of keeping the Gentry and Huntsmen at bay; in a real way, they're extensions of the Gentry and Huntsmen. How would rituals help them here? They don't develop approaches, they use approaches the freehold make.<br /> <br /> I guess what I'm asking is, what's the point of a Loyalist Court? Just the mantle and affinity Contracts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here were my thoughts from the Ogres thread:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/557698-second-edition-ogres?p=564775#post564775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I can see how they might. Loyalists are in league with the Strangers, but that's not really accurate: a <i>particular</i> Loyalist is in league with a <i>particular</i> Stranger. The Gentry aren't all one big happy family, after all. A rival True Fae could well see the Loyalist servants of another as impressive prizes and sources of leverage. I doubt the Huntsmen discriminate between an old master and a prospective one, if the latter can make it worth their while. Given the Strangers' generous definition of sanity, I could even see the Loyalist's own Keeper dispatching a Huntsman, whether as a test to &quot;cull the unworthy,&quot; a punishment for some (quasi-)imagined offense or other anticipated action, or even just a rescinding of the previous distant arrangement and a decision to bring the Loyalist &quot;home.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T06:35:14-07:00","id":566299,"title":"","content":"So, they may be targeted. I still doesn't lend itself to a Court. Loyalists generally won't ally themselves with loyalists of rival fae; hells, the two Loyalists could be set up to be rivals just as much as your example of the Huntsman versus Loyalist. Hells, two Huntsmen from the same True Fae could be subject to the same just as easily. Everything is pointing away from working together as a Court.<br /> <br /> As well, there's the idea that Loyalists, in 1e, were the changelings that infiltrated the freehold Courts from the inside. Having a separate system of Courts would defeat that purpose. It would set them up as rivals to be wary of.<br /> <br /> <br /> From a game design standpoint, what is the purpose of a Loyalist Court system? What does it <i>do</i>? Even more relevantly, if a Court did exist, why should the PCs care? Is it just an added layer of mechanical complexity that's effectively invisible to the player characters? How does it affect game play or the story told during each session?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-24-2015, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T14:17:23-07:00","id":566959,"title":"","content":"My original idea for the Loyalist Court, the one I mentioned in the ogre thread, is indeed that each Fae has its own Court, and all loyalists that serve it have a Mantle, court contracts, and the like. Of course, the true Fae serves as monarch, and it provides no Bulwark, but still. They wouldnt need courts that cross between loyalists of different Keepers, or that serve as social clubs. More like an extension of that Fae's dominion over its slaves. Kith is what makes each Loyalist and free fae unique--the Court provides a narrative connection between slaves of a given Fae, as well as additional benefits to give Loyalists teeth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T14:23:20-07:00","id":566984,"title":"","content":"Fun fact: Courts are built off of stories. True Fae are sometimes called living stories. Work off of that how you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T03:57:57-07:00","id":567621,"title":"","content":"Interesting thought Acanearts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T04:26:11-07:00","id":567635,"title":"","content":"Well, the Gentry serve as a kind of Unseilee Court system to the Lost being the Seilee, so the parallel is there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T08:02:35-07:00","id":567943,"title":"","content":"We're all friends here, call me Arc. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T09:19:10-07:00","id":568056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/566238-loyalist-seeming-courts?p=566299#post566299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, they may be targeted. I still doesn't lend itself to a Court. Loyalists generally won't ally themselves with loyalists of rival fae; hells, the two Loyalists could be set up to be rivals just as much as your example of the Huntsman versus Loyalist. Hells, two Huntsmen from the same True Fae could be subject to the same just as easily. Everything is pointing away from working together as a Court.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not pretending this would be a common arrangement. But there are some interesting possibilities in this sort of thing sometimes arising. That's one of the perks of the Freehold and Court systems being somewhat more personalized: the general trends are away from this sort of thing, but more individual circumstances may well lead to it.<br /> <br /> It provides a different group with very different motives than most Changelings. It may well put PCs in the odd and morally uncomfortable position of disrupting their Bulwark and/or aiding Huntsmen who are after any of its members. There are just some interesting possibilities even in broad strokes.<br /> <br /> I get -- and agree with -- seeing why this wouldn't be a common thing. I just also see nothing to gain by ruling it out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As well, there's the idea that Loyalists, in 1e, were the changelings that infiltrated the freehold Courts from the inside. Having a separate system of Courts would defeat that purpose. It would set them up as rivals to be wary of. </div> </div> </div>I think there's been a misunderstanding of the actual idea. &quot;Some Loyalists are in their own Courts/Freeholds&quot; is not the same as &quot;<i>all</i> Loyalists are <i>only</i> in their own Courts/Freeholds.&quot; Court infiltration will totally still happen. Though it's noteworthy that Court infiltration was never the only purpose Loyalists could serve.<br /> <br /> Loyalists are Changelings who still hold some loyalty and alliance with their Keeper. Privateers are Changelings who actively try to drag other Changelings back to their Keepers. They overlap more than a little on that Venn diagram, but they don't have to do so. There can certainly be Loyalists who don't have anything to do with dragging Changelings back to Arcadia, and instead have other kinds of jobs/tasks in the mortal world for the Gentry they serve.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/566238-loyalist-seeming-courts?p=567635#post567635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Gentry serve as a kind of Unseilee Court system to the Lost being the Seilee, so the parallel is there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I expect it's relevant to the topic of Loyalist Courts, but I do recall some mention in the Court previews of a Seelie/Unseelie Court system. Kinda interested in seeing what form that takes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T12:30:35-07:00","id":568250,"title":"","content":"No problem Arc :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T18:45:30-07:00","id":568595,"title":"","content":"I much prefer the idea of making it a Seeming - as it's the form of your &quot;escape&quot;. i.e. all the Seemings reflect how you changed yourself to survive and escape. The Loyalist Seeming is pretty much Stockholm Syndrome, you changed yourself into a loving extension of your master, and &quot;escaped&quot; at their earned behest.<br /> <br /> Appearance: Kith traits are exaggerated. This can easily lead the assumption a Windwing is a Beast, a Fireheart is an Elemental, etc. You fully embraced and relish what your master made you.<br /> <br /> Blessing: Gain Clarity when you complete a task for your master.<br /> <br /> Curse: Clarity Breaking-point from disobedience or failing a specific ordered task in a way that it can no longer be completed (someone you were meant to retrieve dies, you had a time frame that ran out, etc).<br /> <br /> Seeming Contracts ideas: Like other Seeming Contract Clauses these would be theoretically learnable by others, HOWEVER the theoretical non-Loyalists who somehow found a teacher would lose a point of Clarity every time they use one.<br /> <br /> - Fetch related powers: Sensing, Summoning, Commanding, etc Fetches. Even channeling Echoes (this would allow them to adopt a &quot;False Mien&quot; as need be to fake a specific Seeming); or possibly even creating new Fetches of themselves.<br /> <br /> - Combine the concepts from the First Edition Contract of Thorns &amp; Bramble with the Contract of Lucidity. You can use the thorns of the Hedge to strip away a target's Clarity/Integrity/etc. Possibly even imposing Soullessnes or Thrall Conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T09:26:39-07:00","id":570301,"title":"","content":"I like the appearance being an exageration of your Kith. The Blessing should be more specific, such as gaining a point of Clarity once story when the character succeeds in a way that reinforces the greatness of his master in his eyes. Roll for Clarity lose whenever the character does something that the character feels betrays the interests of they're keeper.<br /> <br /> As for Loyalists Seeming bonus on certain contracts instead of costing a point of clarity, maybe it grants a point of yearning to any Huntsmen hunting the Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}